I was able to make it work without canvas by using [opencv4nodejs](https://github.com/justadudewhohacks/opencv4nodejs) 

```javascript
const cv = require('opencv4nodejs');
const tf = require('@tensorflow/tfjs');
require('@tensorflow/tfjs-node');

const image = 'your image path here';
const mat = cv.imread(image);
// By default opencv is working with BGR color space
// before doing getData, we need to reorganize pixel to RGB
const mat2 = mat.cvtColorAsync(cv.COLOR_BGR2RGB);
const tensor = tf.tensor3d(new Uint8Array(mat2.getData()), [width, height, 3], 'int32').expandDims(0);

net.execute(tensor);
```

