It is not enough to dispose the input tensor, you also have to dispose the layer as follows:

```js
try {
  var input_tensor=await tf.tensor(input_array, random1,random2,random3,random4],"float32");
  layer =  await tf.layers["conv2d"]({filters:3,kernelSize:3,strides:1});
  var prediction = await layer.apply(input_tensor);
  layer.dispose();
  tf.dispose(input_tensor);
} catch (e){
  console.log(e);
}
```

You could also wrap any code that creates layers or tensors in `tf.tidy` if you want to avoid manual disposal.

Let me know if you run into any other issues!

